WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Elena is entitled to a payable life insurance benefit.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.620
A lump sum gives her the benefit in one payment.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.760
Other settlement options may spread proceeds over time, when the contract

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.520
makes them available and any binding owner instructions permit the choice.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.000
A settlement payment option is different from selling a policy to

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.200
an investor during the insured's lifetime.

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.500
Maryland requires a policy offering installments or an annuity to state

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.360
that feature and include determinable payment information.

9
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.740
Begin with the actual contract, eligible payee and payment instructions.

10
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.540
A textbook list of options does not mean every carrier offers

11
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.740
every option on every policy.

12
00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:51.374
Assume an available interest-only arrangement leaves one hundred thousand

13
00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:55.014
dollars with the insurer and pays Elena the interest.

14
00:00:55.654 --> 00:01:00.541
At a hypothetical three percent annual rate, that principal generates three

15
00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:04.994
thousand dollars for a full year under a simple annual calculation.

16
00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:09.874
The payment uses interest rather than deliberately spending down principal.

17
00:01:10.994 --> 00:01:15.494
The contract governs withdrawal access, rate changes and what happens when

18
00:01:15.494 --> 00:01:19.474
Elena dies. Funds retained by an insurer are different from a

19
00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:24.434
bank deposit. Maryland permits the specified proceeds to remain among the

20
00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:28.914
insurer's general assets. Review the insurer's obligations and actual

21
00:01:28.914 --> 00:01:33.054
agreement instead of assuming federal bank-deposit insurance applies.

22
00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:37.756
The beneficiary wants the proceeds distributed over a stated number of

23
00:01:37.756 --> 00:01:42.616
years. Under a fixed-period option, the selected period determines the

24
00:01:42.616 --> 00:01:47.156
payment schedule, while the proceeds and applicable interest help determine

25
00:01:47.156 --> 00:01:51.856
each payment. Use a deliberately simplified example with no interest or

26
00:01:51.856 --> 00:01:56.396
fees: one hundred twenty thousand dollars divided into one hundred twenty

27
00:01:56.396 --> 00:02:00.776
monthly payments produces one thousand dollars per month for ten years.

28
00:02:00.776 --> 00:02:04.816
Real tables can include interest and other contract details.

29
00:02:05.576 --> 00:02:08.996
A fixed ten-year period is not a promise of income for

30
00:02:08.996 --> 00:02:14.276
Elena's entire lifetime. Read the remaining-payment provision if she dies

31
00:02:14.276 --> 00:02:16.236
before the selected period ends.

32
00:02:16.806 --> 00:02:20.506
Now Elena specifies two thousand dollars each month.

33
00:02:21.306 --> 00:02:25.166
Under a fixed-amount option, the chosen payment and the available proceeds

34
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:28.586
with applicable interest determine how long payments continue.

35
00:02:29.146 --> 00:02:32.046
With one hundred twenty thousand dollars and no interest or fees

36
00:02:32.046 --> 00:02:37.706
in this teaching example, the money supplies sixty monthly payments, or

37
00:02:37.706 --> 00:02:41.746
five years. Choosing one thousand dollars instead would make the same

38
00:02:41.746 --> 00:02:44.126
assumed principal last twice as long.

39
00:02:44.946 --> 00:02:47.546
This is not automatically a lifetime guarantee.

40
00:02:48.426 --> 00:02:52.326
Compare it with fixed period by asking what Elena selected first:

41
00:02:53.046 --> 00:02:54.866
the monthly amount or the number of years.

42
00:02:55.266 --> 00:02:58.186
Read how actual credited interest affects the remaining schedule.

43
00:02:58.824 --> 00:03:03.444
A life-income option promises payments for the covered lifetime instead of

44
00:03:03.444 --> 00:03:06.964
merely until a chosen period or fund schedule ends.

45
00:03:07.584 --> 00:03:11.544
A straight single-life form stops when its measuring life dies, with

46
00:03:11.544 --> 00:03:13.284
no additional guarantee assumed.

47
00:03:13.824 --> 00:03:17.464
Life income with a period certain can add minimum remaining payments

48
00:03:17.464 --> 00:03:22.464
under its terms. Joint-and-survivor income uses two lives and continues the

49
00:03:22.464 --> 00:03:24.204
specified payment to the survivor.

50
00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:28.004
The survivor amount may stay the same or be reduced according

51
00:03:28.004 --> 00:03:29.304
to the selected option.

52
00:03:29.624 --> 00:03:33.344
For example, seventy-five percent of a stated two thousand dollar payment

53
00:03:33.344 --> 00:03:34.364
is fifteen hundred dollars.

54
00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:39.044
These are payment forms, not first-death versus second-death life policies.

55
00:03:39.807 --> 00:03:44.587
Do not confuse electing interest-only income with interest owed on an

56
00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:49.547
unpaid death claim. Maryland generally measures interest from the insured's

57
00:03:49.547 --> 00:03:54.487
death until payment. An insurer need not pay that interest when

58
00:03:54.487 --> 00:03:57.067
proceeds are paid within thirty days after death.

59
00:03:57.827 --> 00:04:00.787
If proof of death arrives more than one hundred eighty days

60
00:04:00.787 --> 00:04:05.927
after death, the statutory interest begins when that proof is submitted.

61
00:04:06.587 --> 00:04:09.667
The rate cannot be lower than the insurer's rate on death

62
00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.187
proceeds left on deposit.

63
00:04:11.927 --> 00:04:15.307
These interest rules do not grant permission to delay a valid

64
00:04:15.307 --> 00:04:20.147
claim. Determine the claim dates first, then analyze any later settlement

65
00:04:20.147 --> 00:04:21.207
choice separately.
